  "summary": "Bundled skill scripts contain benign network/CLI usage",
  "details": "The package bundles a collection of 'skills' consisting of helper scripts. The flagged files are: a Python scraper and API server using HTTP GET/POST and 'ping' as part of their documented scraping/API functionality; a benchmark script and verification script that use curl for ordinary HTTP checks; and an install.sh for the rclone-cli skill that runs 'curl https://rclone.org' to install rclone from its official project domain. These are keyword co-occurrences in utility scripts shipped as skill content, not install-time or import-time execution against the installer. package.json does not auto-invoke these scripts; they run only when a user explicitly executes the respective skill. No credential reads, no attacker-controlled destinations, no obfuscation, and no lifecycle hooks fetching remote code were observed.",
